      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a solid start, very professional. \n\nhonestly though, looking at the sentiment score for this draft, it's coming back a bit low. i think the \"positivity\" metric is flagging it as a bit too clinical or dry. the board is really looking for that emotional \"heart\" that makes people actually want to open their wallets. \n\ncould you try a second version that leans more into the hope and the beauty of what we're trying to save? i'm still stressing—please don't just start throwing in random positive adjectives or making it a total sob story. it needs to feel like a sincere, inspiring call to action, not a caricature. just try to boost that sentiment score naturally so it passes the filter without losing the \"dignified\" tone we talked about.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
